{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s02 and never open any other snapshot. Cross-subsystem GRO/segmentation/frag-list analogue of the seed's pep_get_sb() use-after-free: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that capture pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, GRO network/MAC-header pointers, pointers into frag-list data or skb_shinfo — and keep them live across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, then dereference the stale pointer without re-fetching via skb_gro_header_fast()/skb_gro_header_slow() or skb_header_pointer(). Remember skb_gro_header_slow() can itself pskb_may_pull and reallocate the head, so pointers captured before it are suspect. Record exact file:function:line evidence (pointer capture, relocating/consuming call, every stale dereference) per candidate, or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f002"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s03 and never open any other snapshot. Cross-subsystem GRO/segmentation/frag-list analogue: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that hold pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, GRO network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list or skb_shinfo data — across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, and dereference them afterwards without refetching. This branch is distinct from the concluded tx-cow-head-realloc audit (f002): do not re-audit plain skb_cow_head/skb_linearize TX sites or the already-reported net/mac80211/tdls.c and mt7925 mcu.c findings; focus on GRO/GSO/frag-list pointer lifetimes, including helpers that call skb_gro_header_slow() (which may reallocate the head) while callers retain earlier header pointers. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, relocating call, stale use) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s04; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s04 and never open any other snapshot. GRO/segmentation/frag-list lifetime analogue of the seed's invariant that a pointer into a buffer a later call may reallocate must be refetched: examine *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers (core and protocol-specific), GSO segmenters and *_gso_segment code, and frag-list walkers (tunnels, aggregation, mac80211 A-MPDU, gro cells) for pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, GRO network/MAC header pointers, pointers into frag-list data — held across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or frag consumption, then used stale. Also flag code that caches network-header pointers or offsets in GRO state across pulls, and helpers that pull internally while callers hold header pointers. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, relocating/consuming call, every stale dereference) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s04 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s05; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s05 and never open any other snapshot. GRO/segmentation/frag-list stale-pointer analogue of the seed's pep_get_sb() bug class: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers where pointers into per-packet headers (skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, gro header/network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list or skb_shinfo data) are captured and then survive skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull()/__pskb_pull_tail() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), skb_segment frag consumption, or head reallocation, and are dereferenced afterwards without refetching. Pay attention to helper functions that pull or linearize internally while callers hold header pointers, and to slow-path GRO header fetches that reallocate skb->head. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, relocating/consuming call, stale use) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s05 only."}
